---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { site } from '../../data/site';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="HitaruJP | Terms and Conditions"
  description="The terms of use for the HitaruJP Japanese language app: accounts, acceptable use, content and subscriptions."
>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container legal">
      <h1 class="h2">Terms and Conditions</h1>
      <p class="legal-meta">Last updated: October 25, 2026.</p>

      <p class="body-copy">
        These Terms of Service ("Terms") govern your use of HitaruJP, the
        Japanese language-learning app that uses real videos from YouTube, with
        transcripts, AI explanations and spaced-repetition flashcards. They are
        a binding agreement between you and the developer of HitaruJP. The
        Privacy Policy explains how we handle your data; by creating an account
        or using the Service you accept both.
      </p>

      <h2>Acceptance of these Terms</h2>
      <p class="body-copy">
        These Terms of Service ("Terms") are a legally binding agreement between
        you and the developer of HitaruJP ("the Developer", "we", "us", "our").
        They apply whenever you create an account for, sign in to, or otherwise
        use the HitaruJP app and the backend services it relies on.
      </p>
      <p class="body-copy">
        By creating an account, signing in, or otherwise using the Service you
        accept these Terms and the Privacy Policy. If you do not accept them, you
        must not create an account or use the Service.
      </p>
      <p class="body-copy">
        If you use HitaruJP on behalf of a school, club or language programme, you
        confirm that you have authority to accept these Terms on its behalf.
      </p>

      <h2>Eligibility</h2>
      <p class="body-copy">
        You must be at least 13 years old, or the minimum age of digital consent in
        your country where that is higher, and must have the legal capacity to
        agree to a contract. Where local law requires parental or guardian consent
        for users below the age of digital consent, such users may not use
        HitaruJP unless a parent or legal guardian has given consent.
      </p>

      <h2>Your account and security</h2>
      <p class="body-copy">
        You create an account with an email address and password, or by signing
        in with a Google account, through Firebase Authentication. You agree to
        provide accurate account information and to keep your credentials
        confidential. You are responsible for keeping your account and device
        secure and for all activity that happens through your account.
      </p>
      <p class="body-copy">
        You may not create more than one account for yourself, and you may not use
        another person’s account without their permission.
      </p>

      <h2>The service</h2>
      <p class="body-copy">
        HitaruJP provides language learning: curated videos from YouTube matched to
        your level, a tappable transcript, AI explanations, spaced-repetition
        flashcards and reviews, daily recommended videos, and an immersion mode.
        The Service is provided on a best-effort basis and may be added to,
        changed, suspended or discontinued at any time.
      </p>

      <h2>Acceptable use</h2>
      <p class="body-copy">
        You may not use HitaruJP to break the law or these Terms, or to harm the
        Service or other people.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          Scrape, bulk-download or otherwise take the video catalogue beyond the
          way the app is meant to be used.
        </li>
        <li>
          Misuse the AI explanations, or use them to generate content that is
          unlawful, hateful or harmful.
        </li>
        <li>
          Impersonate another learner, language teacher or the HitaruJP team, or
          misrepresent your level, progress or identity.
        </li>
        <li>
          Attempt to gain unauthorised access to accounts, the backend or
          third-party services.
        </li>
        <li>
          Collect or publish another person’s personal information without their
          consent.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Your content and third-party content</h2>
      <p class="body-copy">
        Videos shown in the app belong to their YouTube creators, and the app
        presents them for educational purposes under the creators’ and YouTube’s
        terms. You keep ownership of the sentences, notes and flashcards you save
        yourself; by saving them you grant the Developer the right to store and
        process them for the Service.
      </p>

      <h2>Subscriptions and payments</h2>
      <p class="body-copy">
        HitaruJP may offer subscription tiers that unlock higher levels, more
        daily recommendations or additional features. Where a paid tier is
        offered, the terms of the store you purchase through (Google Play or the
        App Store) apply to the purchase, and the Developer’s own terms apply to
        the Service itself.
      </p>

      <h2>Third-party services</h2>
      <p class="body-copy">
        HitaruJP relies on third-party providers, including Google Firebase for
        authentication and storage, YouTube for videos and transcripts, and the
        AI provider for explanations. Your use of those services is also
        subject to their terms and policies.
      </p>

      <h2>Disclaimers</h2>
      <p class="body-copy">
        The Service is provided "as is" and "as available", without warranties of
        any kind. We do not warrant that the Service will be uninterrupted, secure
        or error-free, or that AI explanations are accurate or complete.
      </p>

      <h2>Limitation of liability</h2>
      <p class="body-copy">
        To the fullest extent permitted by applicable law, the Developer is not
        liable for indirect, incidental, special or consequential damages, or for
        any loss arising from user content, conduct of other users or third-party
        services. The Developer’s total liability for any claim relating to the
        Service is limited to the greater of the fees paid by you for the Service
        in the twelve months before the claim and the minimum amount allowed by
        applicable law.
      </p>

      <h2>Indemnification</h2>
      <p class="body-copy">
        You agree to indemnify and hold the Developer harmless from any claim
        arising out of your content or your breach of these Terms.
      </p>

      <h2>Termination</h2>
      <p class="body-copy">
        You may stop using HitaruJP and delete your account at any time. We may
        suspend or terminate your access to the Service if you breach these
        Terms, with or without notice. The sections that by their nature should
        survive a termination - including the disclaimer of warranties and the
        limitation of liability - survive.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes to these Terms</h2>
      <p class="body-copy">
        We may update these Terms from time to time. The current version is always
        available in the app and is marked with a date. Material changes may
        require you to accept the new Terms. Your continued use of the Service
        after a change takes effect means you accept the updated Terms.
      </p>

      <h2>Governing law and disputes</h2>
      <p class="body-copy">
        These Terms are governed by the laws of the Republic of Malawi, without
        regard to conflict of law rules. Any dispute arising out of or relating to
        these Terms or the Service will be subject to the jurisdiction of the
        courts of Malawi, or to such other dispute resolution mechanism as
        applicable law requires.
      </p>

      <h2>General</h2>
      <p class="body-copy">
        These Terms are the entire agreement between you and the Developer relating
        to the Service, and supersede any earlier agreements. If any provision is
        found unenforceable, the remaining provisions remain in effect. The
        Developer’s failure to enforce a right is not a waiver of it, and the
        Developer may assign these Terms without your consent.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p class="body-copy">
        Email:
        <a class="prose-link" href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>
      </p>
      {
        site.phones.map((phone) => (
          <p class="body-copy">
            Phone:
            <a class="prose-link" href={`tel:${phone.replace(/[^+\d]/g, '')}`}>
              {phone}
            </a>
          </p>
        ))
      }
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .legal {
    display: grid;
    gap: 24px;
    max-width: 70ch;
  }
  /* Quiet section heads: the h1 carries the page scale. */
  .legal h2 {
    font-size: 1.125rem;
  }
  .legal-meta {
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
  }
  /* Bullet list for the acceptable-use rules. */
  .legal ul {
    margin: 0;
    padding-left: 1.25rem;
    display: grid;
    gap: 8px;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 1.0625rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
    max-width: 65ch;
  }
</style>
